{
  "title": "'Customize with AI': make it a small tool-using agent instead of one model call",
  "description": "Depends on customize-1 (frontier model, rename, likely a background job). \
Today custom enrich is one JSON-in/JSON-out call that rewrites the whole recipe (ramekin-core/src/ai/custom_enrich.rs), so the model guesses at things the server knows. \
Make it a bounded tool-calling loop where the model can look things up and then make targeted edits. \
Keep the scope modest. \
Tools worth starting with: look up an ingredient in the catalog (density, piece weights, calories) so 'convert to grams' or 'make it 500 kcal per serving' uses real data; scale the recipe with the existing scaling code; list the user's tags; search the user's other recipes (e.g. 'make the sauce like my other one'); and edit operations (replace an ingredient line, rewrite a step, set a field) in place of returning the whole recipe, so unchanged parts stay byte-identical. \
Cap turns and tool calls, and return the edited recipe as a new version with a short summary of what changed. \
Framework: the server is Rust and talks to OpenRouter through openai-api-rs (ramekin-core/Cargo.toml), whose AiClient has no tool-call support yet. \
Evaluate an existing agent library rather than hand-rolling the loop, e.g. the `rig` crate (tool trait, multi-turn agents, OpenRouter and Anthropic providers), against calling the Anthropic Messages API directly with its tool use. \
Pick one that keeps the response cache and ai-eval harness working, and document the choice in the PR. \
Extend the custom-enrich ai-eval suite with a few cases that need tools (unit conversion with catalog weights, calorie targets). \
Both clients only need progress and summary display changes; no data/ diffs expected.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
